// name :
"P1615276052" "Lost and Found"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PercyHostage 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P22621944" "Circle of Thorns Incantation"
// DetailString :
"P3437083570" "While Percy was held hostage, he managed to steal an old scroll that the Circle of Thorns were using.<br><br>The scroll contains an incantation that appears to directly affect technology. It speaks of taking the power of science and crafting it to the ways of magic. Apparently this was what the Circle was planning on using to bend all origins towards the ways of magic.<br><br>Before Percy left, he told you that the scroll wouldn't actually do what they wanted it to do. They tried the spell, but all it did was turn one of the Circle's books of magic into a cell phone. They threw the scroll away in frustration, which is how Percy managed to get it in the first place."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RiktiIntel1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P671389166" "Rikti Computer Data"
// DetailString :
"P2935657985" "You pull out a handful of what looks like different sized crystals, assuming they must contain some form of information. What you find odd about the crystals is how soft they are to the touch."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RiktiIntel2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1072653679" "You removed what can only be described as a glow net from the under carriage of the computer. There are half a dozen different sized crystals that seem to be growing out of the net."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RiktiIntel3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1046747849" "Reaching your hand into the translucent solution found inside this computer, you come out with a green sphere about the size of a softball. Streaks of electricity shoot around the sphere; it seems to constantly be vibrating."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RiktiIntel4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3652988999" "You try and pull out what looks like a small power source, but when you do, you hear a small chirp and the inside of the computer starts to dissolve like gelatin. Now when you look into the computer case, all you see is a puddle of green goo at the bottom of it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArgotsWork 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P307383448" "Argot'BurWot's Work"
// DetailString :
"P3339711347" "Before he leaves, Argot tells you that he was working on ways to counteract the Rikti's weakness to magic. In his research he used human test subjects. His results were impressive: a human, when given the correct genetic markers, could actually become resistant to a number of different types of biological stimulants. This occurred even on a genetic level. While Argot found the results fascinating, it was not the intended response Argot's keepers were looking for. They threatened his life if he did not produce their results quickly."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Hero1Blood 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2078676561" "A Vial of Blood"
// DetailString :
"P3584802605" "Lady Jane gives you a vial that she says contains blood from Hero 1. This in and of itself isn't that interesting. The interesting part is that she claims it comes from Hero 1 <i>after</i> he entered the Rikti Portal to stop the first Rikti Invasion. She believes that in the right hands, this blood could contain a cure for the Lost."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArgotBloodSample 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1093574609" "Blood Sample"
// DetailString :
"P4267699800" "Argot gave you a sample of the blood he tested from Hero 1. He's altered it to actually reverse the effects of the Lost virus on those already infected. However, currently the virus has very strong blockers in place to prevent this. Argot believes that magic is the answer to this problem. He wants you to seek out Azuria as he believes she will be able to craft something that will bypass the technological barriers in place within the Lost virus."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EmptyWand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P892207044" "Empty Wand"
// DetailString :
"P816299244" "Azuria gave you this wand. To you it looks like a simple stick, but she believes it can hold the serum Argot has created to cure the Lost."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GraveDirt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1924525300" "Midnighter Grave Dirt"
// DetailString :
"P683388427" "Montague gives you a small bowl full of soil. This dirt comes from the grave sites of Midnighters who were killed during the Rikti invasion. It's infused with the angry spirit of all those who were struck down on that fateful day. Their vengeance will guide the wand to the correct target."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LostWand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P246616420" "The Lost Wand"
// DetailString :
"P1874120184" "When you look down at what you made, you see streaks of Rikti energy flowing through the old wooden stick. This wand is a combination of both magic and technology, wield it carefully."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MidnighterClub 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3093660351" "Midnighter Club"
// DetailString :
"P1553933787" "The Midnighter Club is the hidden meeting place for the group known as the Midnight Squad.<br><br>Here they met and discuss matters of the occult and mystics arts. Recently, their attention has turned towards the Rikti. During their first invasion, the Squad was nearly wiped out. The Rikti knew they had a weakness towards magic and therefore attacked magic groups first before all others.<br><br>The Squad has used all of their resources to bolster their ranks and to look at how best to exploit the Rikti's weakness for humanities gain.<br><br>Now the Midnighters have began recruiting both heroes and villains across Paragon City and the Rogue Isle. They're hope... to enlist the power of both sides to seek revenge for the Rikti's first invasion."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2221877385" "The Midnight Squad"
// DetailString :
"P143425082" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3087347957" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you.<br><br>While in the Thorns den, you came across the Lost. This worries the Midnight Squad and so they've diverted their attention to figuring out why the Lost were in that den. You were sent to an abandoned office where recent reports sighted a Lost presence. Montague was unsure what was going on there, but any information regarding the Lost was good information. You went in and found yourself going through a cave network beneath the building. This led you to a large alien room, obviously of Rikti design. Unsure of what you just stepped into, you began gathering as much information as possible. Then you encountered Ci'dion, a Rikti. In his broken language he informed you:<br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'Magic dissolution research: Must progress'</color><br><br>What did he mean by that?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3965217975" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you.<br><br>While in the Thorns den, you came across the Lost. This worries the Midnight Squad and so they've diverted their attention to figuring out why the Lost were in that den. You were sent to an abandoned office where recent reports sighted a Lost presence. Montague was unsure what was going on there, but any information regarding the Lost was good information. You went in and found yourself going through a cave network beneath the building. This led you to a large alien room, obviously of Rikti design. Unsure of what you just stepped into, you began gathering as much information as possible. Then you encountered Ci'dion, a Rikti. In his broken language he informed you:<br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'Magic dissolution research: Must progress'</color><br><br>What did he mean by that?<br><br>The information recovered from the Rikti computers led you to another Rikti research facility where a Rikti scientist, Argot'BurWot was seeking asylum. You went in and got him out, in the process discovering that he was working on a way to counteract the Rikti's weakness to magic."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1306231441" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you.<br><br>While in the Thorns den, you came across the Lost. This worries the Midnight Squad and so they've diverted their attention to figuring out why the Lost were in that den. You were sent to an abandoned office where recent reports sighted a Lost presence. Montague was unsure what was going on there, but any information regarding the Lost was good information. You went in and found yourself going through a cave network beneath the building. This led you to a large alien room, obviously of Rikti design. Unsure of what you just stepped into, you began gathering as much information as possible. Then you encountered Ci'dion, a Rikti. In his broken language he informed you:<br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'Magic dissolution research: Must progress'</color><br><br>What did he mean by that?<br><br>The information recovered from the Rikti computers led you to another Rikti research facility where a Rikti scientist, Argot'BurWot was seeking asylum. You went in and got him out, in the process discovering that he was working on a way to counteract the Rikti's weakness to magic.<br><br>With Argot safely in Vanguard custody, you shifted focus to a visitor from Great Britain. Montague informed you that a member of the Dawn Patrol, named Lady Jane, had come over to the States and was seeking an audience with the Midnight Squad. She was doing her own research on the Lost and wanted to share intel. You tracked her down to an ancient cave filled with ruins from a long lost civilization. For helping her, she gave you a vial of blood. <br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'It's from Hero 1, after he entered the portal to the Rikti homeworld.'</color><br><br>You returned this to Montague, who in turn gave it to Argot'BurWot to see what he could do with it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1581454964" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you.<br><br>While in the Thorns den, you came across the Lost. This worries the Midnight Squad and so they've diverted their attention to figuring out why the Lost were in that den. You were sent to an abandoned office where recent reports sighted a Lost presence. Montague was unsure what was going on there, but any information regarding the Lost was good information. You went in and found yourself going through a cave network beneath the building. This led you to a large alien room, obviously of Rikti design. Unsure of what you just stepped into, you began gathering as much information as possible. Then you encountered Ci'dion, a Rikti. In his broken language he informed you:<br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'Magic dissolution research: Must progress'</color><br><br>What did he mean by that?<br><br>The information recovered from the Rikti computers led you to another Rikti research facility where a Rikti scientist, Argot'BurWot was seeking asylum. You went in and got him out, in the process discovering that he was working on a way to counteract the Rikti's weakness to magic.<br><br>With Argot safely in Vanguard custody, you shifted focus to a visitor from Great Britain. Montague informed you that a member of the Dawn Patrol, named Lady Jane, had come over to the States and was seeking an audience with the Midnight Squad. She was doing her own research on the Lost and wanted to share intel. You tracked her down to an ancient cave filled with ruins from a long lost civilization. For helping her, she gave you a vial of blood. <br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'It's from Hero 1, after he entered the portal to the Rikti homeworld.'</color><br><br>You returned this to Montague, who in turn gave it to Argot'BurWot to see what he could do with it.<br><br>Argot made a discovery. Using the vial of blood and his own research, he figured out how to counteract the Lost virus. The cure had one limitation, however. It couldn't pierce through the technological barriers the Rikti put in place. Argot believed that with the help of magic, you would be able to break through that barrier. You went to Azuria, who gave you a wand she believed would do just that."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission6Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2135335376" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you.<br><br>While in the Thorns den, you came across the Lost. This worries the Midnight Squad and so they've diverted their attention to figuring out why the Lost were in that den. You were sent to an abandoned office where recent reports sighted a Lost presence. Montague was unsure what was going on there, but any information regarding the Lost was good information. You went in and found yourself going through a cave network beneath the building. This led you to a large alien room, obviously of Rikti design. Unsure of what you just stepped into, you began gathering as much information as possible. Then you encountered Ci'dion, a Rikti. In his broken language he informed you:<br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'Magic dissolution research: Must progress'</color><br><br>What did he mean by that?<br><br>The information recovered from the Rikti computers led you to another Rikti research facility where a Rikti scientist, Argot'BurWot was seeking asylum. You went in and got him out, in the process discovering that he was working on a way to counteract the Rikti's weakness to magic.<br><br>With Argot safely in Vanguard custody, you shifted focus to a visitor from Great Britain. Montague informed you that a member of the Dawn Patrol, named Lady Jane, had come over to the States and was seeking an audience with the Midnight Squad. She was doing her own research on the Lost and wanted to share intel. You tracked her down to an ancient cave filled with ruins from a long lost civilization. For helping her, she gave you a vial of blood. <br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'It's from Hero 1, after he entered the portal to the Rikti homeworld.'</color><br><br>You returned this to Montague, who in turn gave it to Argot'BurWot to see what he could do with it.<br><br>Argot made a discovery. Using the vial of blood and his own research, he figured out how to counteract the Lost virus. The cure had one limitation, however. It couldn't pierce through the technological barriers the Rikti put in place. Argot believed that with the help of magic, you would be able to break through that barrier. You went to Azuria, who gave you a wand she believed would do just that.<br><br>You now had all the pieces you needed to craft the Lost Cure. Montague sent you over to the invention table to craft just that. This object is a combination of Rikti technology, magic and the blood of a hero. It takes elements from another continent, another world, another plane of existence, and you to bring it all together."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission7Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3029026918" "Montague Castanella, senior member of the Midnight Squad, sent you into a Circle of Thorns den to rescue Percy Winkley. Apparently Percy, a fellow Midnighter, has a bad habit of getting captured. Once you track down Percy, he hands you a scroll the Circle were using to try and control the flow of magic. Their incantation didn't work and so they threw away the scroll, but Percy picked it up and stashed it. For some reason, he's given it to you.<br><br>While in the Thorns den, you came across the Lost. This worries the Midnight Squad and so they've diverted their attention to figuring out why the Lost were in that den. You were sent to an abandoned office where recent reports sighted a Lost presence. Montague was unsure what was going on there, but any information regarding the Lost was good information. You went in and found yourself going through a cave network beneath the building. This led you to a large alien room, obviously of Rikti design. Unsure of what you just stepped into, you began gathering as much information as possible. Then you encountered Ci'dion, a Rikti. In his broken language he informed you:<br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'Magic dissolution research: Must progress'</color><br><br>What did he mean by that?<br><br>The information recovered from the Rikti computers led you to another Rikti research facility where a Rikti scientist, Argot'BurWot was seeking asylum. You went in and got him out, in the process discovering that he was working on a way to counteract the Rikti's weakness to magic.<br><br>With Argot safely in Vanguard custody, you shifted focus to a visitor from Great Britain. Montague informed you that a member of the Dawn Patrol, named Lady Jane, had come over to the States and was seeking an audience with the Midnight Squad. She was doing her own research on the Lost and wanted to share intel. You tracked her down to an ancient cave filled with ruins from a long lost civilization. For helping her, she gave you a vial of blood. <br><br><color LightSeaGreen>'It's from Hero 1, after he entered the portal to the Rikti homeworld.'</color><br><br>You returned this to Montague, who in turn gave it to Argot'BurWot to see what he could do with it.<br><br>Argot made a discovery. Using the vial of blood and his own research, he figured out how to counteract the Lost virus. The cure had one limitation, however. It couldn't pierce through the technological barriers the Rikti put in place. Argot believed that with the help of magic, you would be able to break through that barrier. You went to Azuria, who gave you a wand she believed would do just that.<br><br>You now had all the pieces you needed to craft the Lost Cure. Montague sent you over to the invention table to craft just that. This object is a combination of Rikti technology, magic and the blood of a hero. It takes elements from another continent, another world, another plane of existence, and you to bring it all together.<br><br>With the Lost Cure crafted, you went to the streets to test it out. One Lost after the next was transformed back into their original self. They came up to you thanking you.<br><br><color orange>You have done what no one ever thought possible. You've brought a cure to the Lost and dealt a deadly blow in the battle against the Rikti.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL2.5-3_SC_Midnight_Squad_StoryArc_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P1844928055" "You look at the drained wand in your hand and are reminded of the events you have come to know of as<br><br><color deepskyblue>Lost and Found</color><br>Montague Castanella came to you and asked you to rescue Percy Winkley, an adventurous lad who often got in over his head. During his rescue in a Circle of Thorns den, you came across some Lost. Percy told you the Lost were looking for something and the Midnight Squad wanted to know what. This led you to an abandoned office where you found a hole that went deep underground. At the end of that twisting cave, you came to a Rikti research facility and came face to face with Ci'dion, a true Rikti. You learned that the Rikti were attempting to remove magic from the world, thereby eliminating their weakness to it. Something had to be done.<br><br>With the help of a Rikti scientist named Argot'BurWot, who was seeking asylum and the new leader of the Dawn Patrol, a woman named Lady Jane, you and the Midnight Squad began to form a plan. You began gathering the pieces you needed to put together a device that would cure the Lost of the Rikti virus, the <color orange>Lost Curing Wand</color>.<br><br>With the wand in hand, you went to the streets and began returning the Lost to the people they once were. With the Lost cured, the Rikti no longer had any control over them. What will the Rikti do without their Lost running around causing havoc, stealing needed supplies and gathering intelligence for them? What effect this will have on the Rikti army?<br><br>Only time will tell."

